{\*\ftnsep\chftnsep}\pgndec\pard\plain \s25\qc\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs56\alang1033\ab\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs56\lang1033\b\qc\ltrpar{
The Salt Road}
\par \pard\plain \s26\qc\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\qc\ltrpar{
A novel}
\par \pard\plain \s1\ilvl0\outlinelevel0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs31\alang1033\ab\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs31\lang1033\b{\listtext\pard\plain \tab}\ls1 \fi0\li0\lin0\fi0\li0\lin0\ltrpar{
The jetty}
\par \pard\plain \s21\fi283\sb0\sa113\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\fi283\sb0\sa113\ltrpar{
Mara came down to the jetty before the light, as she had every morning}{{\super \chftn{\*\footnote \chftn\pard\plain \s28\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs20\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs20\lang1033\ltrpar{
Corran had had no ferry since 1931.}
}}
}{
 since the boats stopped coming. The tide was out and the posts stood up out of the mud like the ribs of something drowned.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\fi283\sb0\sa113\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\fi283\sb0\sa113\ltrpar{
The gulls had gone inland days ago. Nobody in the village said what that meant, though everybody knew it, the way you know the weight of a coat you have worn all winter.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\fi283\sb0\sa113\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\fi283\sb0\sa113\ltrpar{
Down at the slip the old men sat on upturned crates and talked about other years: the year the ice came into the harbour, the year the herring failed, the year the lifeboat went out and came back with no one in it.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\fi283\sb0\sa113\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\fi283\sb0\sa113\ltrpar{
She walked the length of the sea wall and back again, and then once more, because walking was something to do with her hands and her feet while her head went over the same ground it had been over all morning.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\fi283\sb0\sa113\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\fi283\sb0\sa113\ltrpar{
She counted them, as her father had taught her. }{\cs15\i
Nineteen.}{
 There had been twenty the week before.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\fi283\sb0\sa113\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\fi283\sb0\sa113\ltrpar{
Behind her the village was still asleep, its windows dark, its chimneys cold. Only the keeper\u8217\'92s lamp turned on the point, patient as a clock.}
\par \pard\plain \s27\qc\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\qc\ltrpar{
* * *}
\par \pard\plain \s21\fi283\sb0\sa113\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\fi283\sb0\sa113\ltrpar{
By noon the wind had come round to the east and brought the smell of the salt flats with it. Hal found her }{{\*\atrfstart 0}
mending nets}{
}{{\*\atrfend 0}
{{\*\atnid }{\*\atnauthor Ann}\chatn{\*\annotation{\*\atnref 0}{\*\atndate -2014705024}\ltrpar{
Is she alone here? Check against chapter 3.}}} in the lee of the boathouse.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\fi283\sb0\sa113\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\fi283\sb0\sa113\ltrpar{
The gulls had gone inland days ago. Nobody in the village said what that meant, though everybody knew it, the way you know the weight of a coat you have worn all winter.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\fi283\sb0\sa113\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\fi283\sb0\sa113\ltrpar{
Down at the slip the old men sat on upturned crates and talked about other years: the year the ice came into the harbour, the year the herring failed, the year the lifeboat went out and came back with no one in it.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\fi283\sb0\sa113\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\fi283\sb0\sa113\ltrpar{
She walked the length of the sea wall and back again, and then once more, because walking was something to do with her hands and her feet while her head went over the same ground it had been over all morning.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\fi283\sb0\sa113\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\fi283\sb0\sa113\ltrpar{
\u8220\'93}{
They\u8217\'92re saying the road\u8217\'92s gone under at Corran,\u8221\'94 he said. \u8220\'93Three days, maybe four.\u8221\'94}
\par \pard\plain \s21\fi283\sb0\sa113\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\fi283\sb0\sa113\ltrpar{
She didn\u8217\'92t look up. \u8220\'93Then we\u8217\'92ll wait three days.\u8221\'94}
\par \pard\plain \s1\ilvl0\outlinelevel0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs31\alang1033\ab\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs31\lang1033\b{\listtext\pard\plain \tab}\ls1 \fi0\li0\lin0\fi0\li0\lin0\ltrpar{
The tide}
\par \pard\plain \s21\fi283\sb0\sa113\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\fi283\sb0\sa113\ltrpar{
The water rose all afternoon. It came in over the flats in long grey sheets, quiet as breathing, and filled the channels one by one until the jetty stood in open water.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\fi283\sb0\sa113\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\fi283\sb0\sa113\ltrpar{
The gulls had gone inland days ago. Nobody in the village said what that meant, though everybody knew it, the way you know the weight of a coat you have worn all winter.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\fi283\sb0\sa113\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\fi283\sb0\sa113\ltrpar{
Down at the slip the old men sat on upturned crates and talked about other years: the year the ice came into the harbour, the year the herring failed, the year the lifeboat went out and came back with no one in it.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\fi283\sb0\sa113\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\fi283\sb0\sa113\ltrpar{
She walked the length of the sea wall and back again, and then once more, because walking was something to do with her hands and her feet while her head went over the same ground it had been over all morning.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\fi283\sb0\sa113\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\fi283\sb0\sa113\ltrpar{
Mara watched it from the window of the net loft. She had seen spring tides }{\revised\revauth1\revdttm-2014705024 
many times }{
before, and storm tides, but never one that came in so }{\cs15\i
smoothly}{
, }{\deleted\revauthdel1\revdttmdel-2014705024 
and so fast, }{
as if it had somewhere to be.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\fi283\sb0\sa113\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\fi283\sb0\sa113\ltrpar{
At six the keeper rang the bell.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\fi283\sb0\sa113\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af5\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af6\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\fi283\sb0\sa113\ltrpar{
